<title>BULGARIA: Yield falls to 3.69 pct on Bulgaria 4-wk T-bills.</title>
<headline>Yield falls to 3.69 pct on Bulgaria 4-wk T-bills.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Yield fell further on Bulgaria's Finance Ministry four-week discount T-bills at the daily auction on Tuesday as the issue was oversubscribed, central bank figures showed.</p>
<p>The average yield to maturity on the issue was 3.69 percent, down from 3.77 percent at Monday's auction and 3.81 percent on Friday.</p>
<p>Details of the issue follow. Prices in percent of par:</p>
<p> Issue number		  BG3037397000</p>
<p> Maturity			four weeks</p>
<p> Par value		     24,000 million levs</p>
<p> Issue date		    June 4</p>
<p> Maturity date		 July 2</p>
<p> Bids received		 33,231.7 million levs</p>
<p> Avg price of bids	   96.42 pct</p>
<p> Bids approved		 24,000 million levs</p>
<p> Avg accepted price	  96.44 pct</p>
<p> Avg yield to maturity     3.69 pct</p>
<p>-- Sofia Newsroom, (++359-2) 91188</p>
</text>
